Not covered by the GHCR generated bundle: the Tauri desktop Cargo graph,
the React Native npm graph, CocoaPods/native notices, and the retired
SwiftPM snapshot (kept only as history in legal/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
The React Native graph is license-gated in full by
scripts/check_npm_licenses.mjs; direct phone dependencies that an ADR
introduced are named in legal/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md ("Phone client
direct additions"), currently expo-blur (MIT, ADR-0189), expo-haptics and expo-glass-effect
(MIT, #3580) and the Lucide
icon paths (ISC) rasterized into clients/mobile/src/design/icons.
Direct desktop dependencies an ADR introduced are named there too
("Desktop client direct additions"), currently portable-pty (MIT,
ADR-0190) and libc (MIT OR Apache-2.0); the Tauri desktop Cargo graph
is license-gated by scripts/check_cargo_licenses.sh.

Direct server dependencies an ADR introduced are named in
legal/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md ("Server direct additions"), currently p256
(Apache-2.0 OR MIT) and unicode-normalization (MIT OR Apache-2.0),
ADR-0146 amendment 2026-09-28; both are also in the generated bundle.

The agent-worker image also carries a local sentence-embedding model and ONNX Runtime for team-memory
search (ADR-0196 D8 증보, #3173): intfloat/multilingual-e5-small weights (MIT, unmodified int8 ONNX
published by the model authors) and ONNX Runtime (MIT, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation; the
unmodified shared library, loaded through the ort and fastembed crates, with Microsoft's own
ThirdPartyNotices.txt under /usr/share/licenses/momo-rust/onnxruntime/). They are not Cargo crates,
so the generated bundle cannot list them; legal/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md ("Embedded model and ONNX
Runtime") carries their notices.

Team memory v2 (ADR-0196 D2) adapts prompt wording and design ideas from company-brain
(Supermemory Inc., Apache-2.0), mem0 (Mem0, Inc., Apache-2.0), Hindsight (Vectorize AI, Inc.,
MIT: Copyright (c) 2025 Vectorize AI, Inc.) and Graphiti (Zep Software, Inc., Apache-2.0); no
upstream code is copied. The consolidation job re-implements Hindsight's consolidation flow and
Graphiti's contradiction/interval-closing rule over PostgreSQL.
The attribution table is legal/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md ("Adapted designs and prompts").

Named runtime companions operators actually run next to these images:

- PostgreSQL 18 (PostgreSQL License)
- pgvector (PostgreSQL License)
- pgBackRest (MIT)
- libssh2 (BSD-3-Clause/ISC)
- Centrifugo v6 (companion service; not baked into the app image)
